and the  bipartisan infrastructure law that was  signed invests a significant amount of  money to move in that direction do you  see this as a silver lining then to the  pain many americans are feeling it'll  accelerate the movement i don't think  there's a silver lining i don't think  there's pain does not have a silver  lining it is painful but i do know that  countries are accelerating um that  toward clean energy i mean europe has  got a whole strategy about moving away  from russian fossil fuels and moving  away from fossil fuels altogether and i  think that's a good thing ultimately but  nobody wants to take any silver lining  or any pleasure at all in what people  are paying at the pump  secretary grant home thank you so much  we appreciate you
 

